# VISUAL CHECK (mandatory if the wave touches UI: .pug/.html/.scss/.css/components)
grep + build only prove the code is THERE, not that it LOOKS right — they never catch real width,
wrong-language text, or overflow/overlap. Before marking a UI task completed, render the page in headless
Chrome and review the screenshot YOURSELF:
- Render against a local server (full env) or, if it can't boot, the deployed URL.
- Screenshot with a headless-Chrome helper (Playwright/Puppeteer + the system browser, e.g.
  `node {{repo}}/scripts/shot.cjs <url> <out.png> [lang] [width]`). Capture desktop (≥1280) AND mobile (375);
  both languages if the app is i18n. {{If the project has no screenshot helper, the FIRST UI task creates one.}}
- Read the PNG and verify: width/responsive (not "compacted"), i18n correct, no overlaps, design-system
  fonts/colors. Only then mark the UI task completed.

